    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n40634" root="نهر" body-key="n">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَهَرٌ</span></b> : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَهْرٌ</span>, in two places. ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  <i>Amplitude:</i>
(K:) or <i>light and amplitude:</i> so, accord. to
some, in the Kur, liv. 54, differently explained
above: see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَهْرٌ</span>, (S, TA.) or, accord. to Th, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَهَر</span>
is a pl. [or rather quasi pl.] of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نُهُرٌ</span>, which is a pl.
of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نهَارٌ</span>. (TA.)

